   $q$Which feature of early movies do both texts describe?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Printed programs that listed the name of each musician.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Actors who spoke their lines aloud from behind the screen.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Film reels that broke and ended every show early.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Live piano music that played along with silent films.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Live piano music that played along with silent films.$q$, $q$Ines plays below the screen in Text 1, and the poem's speaker hears "a player" whose music "runs beside the film." The poem says "no actor speaks," so spoken lines are wrong.$q$, 'draft', 'aa3d9918-1a09-5b51-9564-9a23ceabc5f9')
