   $q$How do the points of view of the two texts differ?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Text 1 shows the audience's feelings only, while Text 2 explains how the pianist chooses each piece of music.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-texts"},{"text":"Both texts are told by the projectionist, who sees both the pianist and the audience from the back of the hall.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Text 1 is told by an audience member, while Text 2 is spoken by the pianist describing her own hands and work.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-point-of-view"},{"text":"Text 1 shows the pianist's effort and choices, while Text 2 shows only the music's effect on a listener who never learns her name.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Text 1 shows the pianist's effort and choices, while Text 2 shows only the music's effect on a listener who never learns her name.$q$, $q$Text 1 follows Ines as she chooses marches and waltzes and feels her hands ache, while the poem's speaker hears a player "whose name I never learn." The poem never explains how the music is chosen.$q$, 'draft', 'aa3d9918-1a09-5b51-9564-9a23ceabc5f9')
