   $q$What do both texts show the new radio doing?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Replacing newspapers as the only way to learn the baseball scores.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Teaching listeners how to repair farm machinery and buildings.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Keeping people indoors and away from their friends and family.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"Drawing people together to share something broadcast from far away.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Drawing people together to share something broadcast from far away.$q$, $q$The Lindqvists crowd into the kitchen for weather and music, and the tenants gather on the stairs for a game. The radio brings people together in both texts rather than isolating them.$q$, 'draft', '9d8c393f-48bf-5db3-a6a5-09caa47c9f27')
