  ('a8773fa7-905f-5989-8e2f-d6b8aa0e89a3', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-comparing-texts'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The frost warning in Text 1 has no counterpart in Text 2. What does this difference suggest about how each text treats the radio?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Text 1 presents the radio as a practical tool for rural work as well as a pleasure, while Text 2 treats it as shared entertainment and company.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Text 1 presents the radio as useless for entertainment, while Text 2 presents it as useless for anything except weather.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Text 1 presents the radio as dangerous to farmers, while Text 2 presents it as safe because city weather is always mild.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The difference shows that the two texts must come from different decades, since weather reports did not exist in the city.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Text 1 presents the radio as a practical tool for rural work as well as a pleasure, while Text 2 treats it as shared entertainment and company.$q$, $q$Hearing "frost on Thursday" lets Papa save the tomatoes, a working use, while the tenants gather for a game and later just for company. Text 1 also includes a string quartet, so it does not treat the radio as useless for entertainment.$q$, 'draft', '9d8c393f-48bf-5db3-a6a5-09caa47c9f27')
