   $q$How do the two texts differ in when the planters expect to see the benefit of their work?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Nadia expects nothing to grow for many generations, while the poem's speaker sees full shade by the end of the summer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-texts"},{"text":"Both planters expect the trees to stop the wind completely within a single week of planting.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Nadia sees small signs of progress within one summer, while the poem's speaker expects the benefit to come after his or her own lifetime.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Neither planter expects any benefit, since both believe the saplings will certainly die.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Nadia sees small signs of progress within one summer, while the poem's speaker expects the benefit to come after his or her own lifetime.$q$, $q$By August Nadia feels damper soil and sees the height marks rise, while the speaker says "I will not sit beneath its shade" and imagines "some child I will never meet." Neither expects instant results.$q$, 'draft', '10e9d0cb-9c22-509a-b6de-4a81b532ed66')
