   $q$Which theme do the two texts share?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Calculators are harmful and should be kept out of classrooms and shops entirely.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstatement"},{"text":"Speed is the most important quality in solving any kind of math problem.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"Older people understand technology better than younger people in every situation.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"A calculator is a useful tool, but people still need to understand math for themselves.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A calculator is a useful tool, but people still need to understand math for themselves.$q$, $q$The teacher keeps the calculators but adds estimates, and the grandmother calls the calculator "a fine helper." Neither text bans the tool, so the choice calling it harmful overstates both.$q$, 'draft', '770edf92-39d2-5474-8e4f-c7f78e730283')
