   $q$How do the two adults' attitudes toward the calculator differ at the start of each text?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Both adults are equally wary and agree to use calculators only after a long petition.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The teacher is wary and leaves the box unopened, while the grandmother is impressed and eager to try it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Both adults are delighted at first and lose interest only after the batteries die.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The teacher is eager to use the calculators, while the grandmother refuses to touch the machine at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-texts"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The teacher is wary and leaves the box unopened, while the grandmother is impressed and eager to try it.$q$, $q$Ms. Abernathy-Reyes leaves the box unopened "for a full week," while the grandmother "was impressed" and borrows it for the shop. Only the students write a petition, and only in Text 1.$q$, 'draft', '770edf92-39d2-5474-8e4f-c7f78e730283')
