   $q$How do the two texts reach their shared lesson through different kinds of events?$q$, $q$[{"text":"In Text 1 the calculator works but gives absurd answers from wrong inputs, while in Text 2 the calculator stops working and human skill takes over.","is_correct":true},{"text":"In both texts the calculator breaks at an important moment, so both lessons are about the poor quality of early machines.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"In Text 1 the calculator's batteries die during class, while in Text 2 the grandmother enters the wrong numbers and gets an absurd total.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-texts"},{"text":"In both texts a student teaches an adult to use mental math, so the lessons come from young people rather than elders.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$In Text 1 the calculator works but gives absurd answers from wrong inputs, while in Text 2 the calculator stops working and human skill takes over.$q$, $q$Raul and Hana "pressed the keys correctly" but entered the wrong numbers, while in Text 2 "the batteries died" and the grandmother works the totals by hand. In Text 1 nothing breaks, so the lessons do not both come from faulty machines.$q$, 'draft', '770edf92-39d2-5474-8e4f-c7f78e730283')
